i more courage to leave here. Whether I can play that role is still a question\u2026\"\n[2401] Hakamura looked a little embarrassed, while Yuki fidgeted with her shoulders. I understood her feelings. [2402] \"So what about me, Akane?\" Kotoha asked, adjusting her glasses and showing no emotion on her face. [2403] On the other hand, Akane seemed to be getting annoyed with the constant requests from different people. She sipped her coffee as if waiting for someone to respond to her. [2404] \"Please put on that badge or whatever. I've clearly expressed my opinion. When the Abeno family announced their engagement two days ago, I said I didn't like having tourists here. You remember that, don't you?\" [2405] Perhaps due to her seniority, Kotoha's immovable demeanor made Akane nod silently. It seemed she had completely retreated to a defensive position. [2406] \"I didn't have any intention to kill Nao. Even if I did, moving the body would have been a problem, let alone lifting it to a high place,\" Ai calmly explained her innocence. [2407] Although I had no idea what was going on, the repeated mention of the word \"kill\" stabbed at my chest. [2408] Just then, two people almost simultaneously exclaimed \"What?\". [2409] \"Didn't you hear it?\" Hachikura asked, looking around at everyone. \"There seems to be some strange sound coming from the other side of the river.\" [2410] \"It sounds like a landslide,\" said Jouken-sensei. However, no one, including me, noticed it. [2411] \"Probably just a figment of the imagination,\" Kikyo coldly said, likely disliking the pause in the conversation. [2412] The sound the two heard was considered a hallucination, and the conversation continued. [2413] \"What do you think of Kono's ambition?\" asked Yoshinobu. He probably stepped in to support his wife's weakening stance. [2414] \"I can only say that I have no comment.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 6:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nHe said it was a war trophy he won when he played cards with American soldiers in Yokosuka.\" [4266] \"That's quite ruthless!\" [4267] I could hear their back-and-forth conversation. How could they be so calm? It made me uneasy. [4268] Suddenly, I smelled a fragrance reminiscent of freshly grown grass. It was the scent that had been wafting from within the room since I opened the door. [4269] \"Jiang Goda!\" I called out from the shadows by the door. [4270] \"What is it?\" [4271] \"There's a grassy scent. What is it?\" Although I ask aloud, I already have a hunch. [4272] \"It's the same here as at the scene where Mr. Onizuka was killed. It seems to be sprinkled all over with that perfume called 'Full'.\" [4273] Just as I thought. [4274] \"So, it's on Noguchi-san, right?\" [4275] \"Yes... and on the piano keys as well.\" [4276] What's going on here? Professor Kawai gave a reasonable explanation for the scene of Mr. Onizuka's murder being covered in the same perfume as his name - the perfume was like Ariadne's thread, spreading throughout the labyrinthine cave of darkness, laid by the murderer to follow the victim. Why is it happening again here? It's really puzzling. [4277] More importantly, who killed Higashizawa? I know it's not the same killer who killed Mr. Onizuka because Mr. Onizuka wasn't killed by anyone else, but by Higashizawa himself. After we confirmed that Higashizawa was the murderer, we thought the case was closed, but now he's been killed. It leaves us in confusion again. It's like being car sick, completely baffled by this mystery. [4278] They came out. As we stood half-opened the door, waiting, a group of people came up from downstairs. [4279] \"Is Higashizawa really dead?\" As he approached us, walking at the front, Koujou asked. His face showed a stiff and tense expression. [4280] \"He's dead, and it was a murder,\" Professor Kawai opened the door to let everyone see the room inside. Koujou, the Fukuda couple, Yuki, Kikko, and Koto looked around the room like visitors to a private museum, one after another, and then stepped back. [4281] - Aki is not here. [4282] I relaxed for a moment before I realized something was wrong. [4283] \"What's going on? Is the target not just Kono?\" asked Mr. Maeda, trembling his lips. He must have been intertwined with anger, sadness, and fear. [4284] \"After Kono, it will be Higuchi,\" muttered Tsuru. Compared to Mr. Maeda, she seemed quite calm. Rather than being calm, perhaps it would be better to say that she had numbed her emotions. I speculated: She was actually worried. [4285] \"Ms. Kisshimoto,\" called Professor Jiang, and Koto looked up. \"There's something I need to ask you. Please smell to see if anyone here has the scent of your 'Full' perfume.\" [4286] \"What's going on?\" Kou asked. [4287] Kiku immediately sensed Jinguji's intentions. \"There's a scent of 'Full' in the music room. The killer must have sprinkled my perfume there again, so you think the killer still has some residual scent on them!\" she said. [4288] \"Yes. And this time it's different from the previous incident. It hasn't been long since the crime was committed. If the creator of 'Full,' who has the most sensitive nose of anyone, Ms. Kusaka, perhaps you can detect the residual scent the killer inadvertently left on themselves\u2026\"\n[4289] \"You want me to smell everyone's scent one by one?\" Kiku's red lips trembled slightly as she asked. Her tone was not very friendly, and perhaps she felt hurt. [4290] \"I know it's rude to both Ms. Kusaka and the others,\" Jinguji said, not elaborating further. Perhaps he thought it would be even ruder to continue. [4291] \"I don't care,\" Qin Gui agreed, \"If everyone allows it, I can play the role of a dog; only I'm not sure if it will be effective.\" [4292] \"First, try me and Mr. Zhidu,\" Jiang Shen skipped the process of seeking permission from others, he pushed Zhidu and walked up himself. Zhidu wanted to say something but remained silent. [4293] \"You're afraid that the smell will fade away if we don't hurry?\" Qin Gui said, leaning her face close to Jiang Shen's shoulder, and shrugged her nose. [4294] \"Yes,\" Jiang Shen answered close to Qin Gui's head, his tone clearly showing impatience. [4295] \"Your head turns well,\" Qin Gui said, not whether she was praising or teasing, \"However...well, how do you say it? The residual fragrance of 'full' is much weaker than that of 'bodhi'. Extend your hand. The killer should have opened the bottle with his hand.\" [4296] Jiang Godong obediently did as he was told. The perfume artist took his hand and carefully sniffed the scent. [4297] \"You grew up near the ocean, didn't you?\" Jiang Godong's expression wavered slightly when he was unexpectedly pointed out, \"You have a distant scent of sea tides, which is a unique smell for people who grew up by the seaside.\" [4298] Jiang Godong smiled, \"Please don't joke around.\" [4299] Qin Gui suddenly let go of his hand, a smile playing on her face, \"I apologize, now is not the time for pranks. I can't smell the scent of 'Fulai' on you.\" [4300] Jiang Godong glanced at Zhu, who silently extended his hands to Qin Gui. As she sniffed his hands seriously, Zhu remained tense and motionless. [4301] \"It's not you either.\" [4302] Before she asks who the next one is, I step forward and say, \"Excuse me!\" Although it was only ten seconds, it was still uncomfortable to have someone sniffing around you. [4303] Next came Kiku, Kouzo, and so on. Everyone walked up to Qin Hui one by one. Although no one objected, no one expressed agreement either. [4304] \"I'm sorry, Jian Shenxiang, I don't know. Although I thought that the murderer might have washed his hands with soap to remove the scent, no one has any suspicions. Although the perfumer's sense of smell is a million times higher than that of an ordinary person...\"\n[4305] \"Maybe the murderer wore gloves.\" Jian Shenxiang adds this remark and thanks Qin Hui. [4306] \"Call Yukiho here. If she didn't undergo the test, it wouldn't be fair, right?\" [4307] Philo's words remind me of Yukiho, who is not present. The sense of security I had just a moment ago has vanished, and unease spreads like a giant bird's shadow over my heart. [4308] \"Where is Yukiho?\" I ask myself. [4309] Philo shakes her head. \"She went for a walk! She said she wanted to feel the fresh air outside.\" [4310] \"A walk... \"\n[4311] \"Chizu and I even told her that dinner was all set\u2026 Oh?\" [4312] Zhezi looked over my shoulder at the other end of the corridor. The sound of someone climbing the stairs could be heard. [4313] \"It seems she's already home.\" Zhezi's voice sounded very calm. [4314] I rushed out of the corridor. \"Yuki! Wait!\" [4315] Yuki appeared, seemingly surprised to see everyone gathered on the upper floor. [4316] \"What's going on?\" [4317] She has a \"What's wrong?\" expression, seemingly unaware of anything out of the ordinary. I run towards her, despite my sadness. [4318] \"What's wrong? Masaya?\" [4319] I suddenly stop in front of her and take a deep breath. [4320] - Why is it up to me to convey this? [4321] I regretfully told her about Akiyoshi's death. [4322] Miyuki suddenly lost consciousness and collapsed. [4323] \"Someone help!\" [4324] As I turned back and called for help, a wave of dizziness hit me, and I fell down. I saw the silhouette of the Kawaoka-sensei running towards me. [4325] 2\n[4326] The sun had set. Six candles on the table flickered. The dimness of the room corner, in sync with the flickering rhythm, stirred\u2026\n[4327] A simple dinner ended. I could hardly eat, and I wondered if the others felt the same way. Would they force themselves to swallow food while feeling pain\u2026\n[4328] The woman in black, Katsuko, entered the room. \"It seems that the sedative has taken effect, and she is sleeping soundly.\" [4329] \"Yes, it's for the best for the child,\" said Kimi. [4330] Katsuko sat down in the empty seat next to me and whispered, \"Are you okay, Matsuri?\" [4331] I reply, \"Yes.\" [4332] \"I'm worried about Yuki, but please pull yourself together. How could you both faint?\" [4333] \"I apologize for scaring everyone. I suddenly felt dizzy in my head and couldn't stand. I'm fine now.\" [4334] \"I wish that were the case,\" the woman says, giving my hand on the table a light squeeze. [4335] Everyone is gathered except Yuki. Zeshi's strong voice speaks up, \"I have a question for the lady.\" [4336] \"What is it, Tsubaki?\" [4337] \"When we found the body of Kurosawa-san, you set a two-day deadline for us to delay contacting the outside world. The two-day deadline ends tonight. What should we do tomorrow morning? Should we ask for help from outside, or do you plan to extend the deadline again by citing a new event? That's what we want to know.\" [4338] Despite her pale face, Kikuha quickly responded, \"I certainly won't extend the time. If another murder were to occur, it would be disastrous. I can't help but feel regretful, thinking that if I hadn't said what I did, Kurosawa-san might not have been killed.\" [4339] Kikuha's closest in age, Koyuki gently placed her hand on Kikuha's shoulder to comfort her. [4340] \"So, we'll seek help from outside tomorrow?\" Tsubaki confirmed again. [4341] \"Yes. It's already late tonight, so let's wait until tomorrow morning,\" Kiku said. [4342] \"Should we gather in the living room until dawn?\" Shoko asked. [4343] Kiko replied that it wasn't necessary, \"If we block the door with the bed, it doesn't matter if we don't lock it. Since we're already tired, there's no need to stay up late. Right, husband?\" [4344] Kiko's husband, Kikuo, nodded obediently. It turns out that this couple, like me, uses locking the door as a form of self-defense. [4345] \"Is it okay to start a detective meeting to find out who killed Akutsu-san?\" [4346] Zhuo's words seemed insensitive to the group, including me, who had no energy to discuss such matters. [4347] \"If we knew who the killer was, wouldn't we be able to sleep soundly after tying them up?\" asked Zhuo. [4348] \"You! Even at the end, you're still so stubborn!\" Chieko teased, \"The detective game is over. We failed.\" [4349] The word \"failure\" struck me deeply. [4350] - Have we really failed? [4351] The dean pointed out that the killer of Kono was Hakamura, and I understood that, so the detective should have won. Do we have to swallow this failure now? [4352] - Perhaps Hakamura is not the killer? [4353] Just as I was pondering this, Shouko's voice interrupted my thoughts. [4354] \"Even if it's just for fun, let's review this incident. Maybe we can catch the killer's tail.\" [4355] \"Is that so? We've already mentioned the interesting idea that 'the scent of the perfume might still be on the killer.' But we haven't found anything yet. I don't think the killer would easily reveal a weakness.\" [4356] When Jang Sun-sang helped Yuri, who was shocked and lost her mind, to stand up, Kiyoharu sniffed Yuri's hands first. Although it's good to judge her innocent, Kiyoharu's feelings must have been extraordinary. [4357] \"Unlike last time, this time the crime time can be locked. Perhaps by investigating the alibi, we may unexpectedly find some clues.\" [4358] \"Kyoko, I envy your optimism!\" [4359] Kyoko didn't get angry at Yuri's words. It's probably difficult to gather evidence if a person like him commits a crime. When I thought of this, I shook my head because I didn't doubt this dancer's words. [4360] \"Well, let's start. I have something to say.\" Yuri took a drag on her cigarette. Normally, Kiyoharu would protest, but tonight she remained silent. [4361] \"Hakozaki entered the music room at 3:30 PM. Before that, I had coffee with him. Ura-Harumi and my husband were also present.\" [4362] \"I was there too,\" Xiao Ling said. [4363] \"Yes, that's right. There were five people. It was said that Hakozaki accompanied Ura-Harumi's singing practice before that, and he said he wanted to play his own piece after having coffee.\" [4364] Zhe Zi and Xiao Ling nodded. [4365] \"Hakozaki said, 'I'm going to play the piano,' and left the restaurant. It was around 3:30 PM.\" [4366] After hearing this, I spoke up, \"I saw Atakuma leaving the restaurant.\" [4367] \"Around 3:30 PM?\" asked Chie. [4368] \"Yes. I picked a book from the library and was heading back to my room when I met him at the bottom of the stairs, so we went up together.\" [4369] \"Did you see him enter the music room?\" asked Kikuko immediately. [4370] \"Yes. My room is across from the music room, so we said goodbye at the door. Then, I saw him enter the music room.\" [4371] \"Did anyone else see him alive after that?\" No one answered Kikuyo's question. [4372] \"The time the body was found was 5:00,\" said Jotaro confidently. \"So the time of the crime was between 3:30 and 5:00. Let's check alibis in that time frame, shall we? Start with you, Jinguji-senpai.\" [4373] Jinguji-senpai, who had been silent until now, slowly spoke, \"Until 3:00, I was with Mashiroya. Hokuzawa and the others invited me to have coffee, but I declined because I was sleepy and wanted to take a nap, so I went back to my room. Mashiroya said she wanted to see a book and went to the library, and we parted ways downstairs.\" [4374] But I don't know what Jinguji-senpai did after that. [4375] \"As soon as I got back to my room, I lay down on the bed. When I was about to fall asleep and my eyelids were getting heavy, I heard someone knocking on the door.\" [4376] \"It turns out you were going to take a nap at that time?\" Shizuka lowered her head to the dean sitting next to me on my right. It was Shizuka who knocked on the door. [4377] \"You don't have to apologize,\" the dean said mildly. [4378] \"Why did you want to find Mr. Kouji?\" Zetsu asked curiously. [4379] The dean looked at the inquirer's eyes and answered, \"When Mashiroya and I came back from exploring the cave, the walking Miss Sawamura saw us, so she came to ask if I had any discoveries.\" [4380] \"I came back from walking and went back to my room, but I was very bothered by the sight of Mr. Kouji and Mashiroya from afar...\"\n[4381] \"Oh, I see. What exactly bothered you?\" [4382] \"Because both of your expressions were so serious, and... it seemed like you were hiding something important. So, I thought something must have happened.\" [4383] Yuki's insight impressed me. Perhaps there was an unusual atmosphere around us at that time, and we didn't even notice someone watching us. [4384] However, how did Jang Godfather respond to Yuki's question? [4385] He spoke again: \"I'm sorry, but we didn't make any major discoveries to report to everyone. I may have disappointed Miss Suzuki, but she didn't show any signs of dissatisfaction and even invited me, 'Would you like to come to my studio?'.\" [4386] This startled me. Had J\u014dg\u014d sensei seen Miyuki's portrait of me? The thought made my face flush with embarrassment. [4387] \"Miyuki, I'm sorry!\" [4388] \"What?\" [4389] Miyuki stared at me. \"I took the liberty of showing J\u014dg\u014d-sensei your portrait.\" [4390] \"Oh\u2026\"\n[4391] Indeed! [4392] \"I didn't just show it to him on a whim! I wanted someone who knows you to take a look and give me their opinion. If there's anything I've missed, I wanted to ask them to correct me. That's why\u2026\"\n[4393] \"Hmm.\" [4394] \"Mr. Jiang also said, 'Should I wait until Maria knows?' But I still asked him to take a look right away.\" [4395] \"I won't mind.\" [4396] What else could I say? Even if the painting was of me, it's still her work! It's just that the exposure of my legs in the painting was a bit too much, which made me a little embarrassed. It's strange! There's no need to care so much, maybe because I never thought that portrait would be seen by Jiang Shen's elder brother! [4397] \"It's a great painting!\" Jiang Shen's elder brother only said that one sentence. My face immediately turned red. [4398] \"Were you two in the studio the whole time?\" Shizuka asked formally.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 7:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nCan we track in the dark labyrinth without Ariadne's thread - the scent? After the experiment, the answer is no.\" [3817] I looked at Mr. Shiro's poetry collection again. Just as I randomly picked up this book and was moved by how good the poem was, Mr. Jiang had already started to wind up Ariadne's thread. Even though he knew that the place we arrived at was worth mentioning, he didn't even let us see the action of winding the thread. He's always like that. [3818] \"So, the killer is someone who knows Mr. Onizuka has anosmia, right?\" [3819] \"Yes.\" [3820] I recalled Mr. Jiang asking everyone at lunch who knew Mr. Onizuka had anosmia. However... \"It's hard to determine who knows and who doesn't, because the killer may have concealed that he knows this information.\" [3821] \"That's right. Even if we know that the killer knows that Mr. Onizuka has anosmia, we can't determine who it is.\" [3822] Has the journey of reasoning come to an end? No, the Dean of Jiang said \"knows who the killer is,\" didn't he? [3823] The Dean of Jiang lit a second cigarette. The smoke was blown out, but it returned along the same path. [3824] \"The killer sprinkled 'bog tree' on the items Mr. Onizuka carried to create a scent trail, leading to - literally - Mr. Onizuka's studio, and then sneaked up behind him, who was immersed in his work, and killed him without anyone disturbing him. To hide the unnatural scent of the victim's belongings and avoid suspicion of the crime, the killer sprinkled the same perfume on the surroundings and the corpse, exaggerating the situation and changing the truth.\" [3825] No need to review! Even after hearing this, I still can't identify the killer. I wish I could make progress faster...\n[3826] \"The person who could have sprinkled perfume on Mr. Onizuka's belongings is the killer.\" Professor Kuroda slowly speaks, and I urge him to continue, \"When and how was the perfume sprinkled on Mr. Onizuka's things?\" [3827] Since he speaks slowly, I blurt out, \"Of course, it was before entering the cave!\" [3828] \"That's right, it was before Mr. Onizuka entered the cave. We passed by Mr. Onizuka, who was carrying a handbag full of paint supplies and humming his way to his studio - as I mentioned earlier - without smelling anything. The perfume was sprinkled afterward, after Mr. Onizuka went downstairs. During the time between Mr. Onizuka going downstairs and entering the cave, the killer sprinkled perfume on the items he was carrying. That is the conclusion we have reached here.\" [3829] \"The one who can do that is\u2026\"\n[3830] \"It's Hakamura who was in the kitchen.\" [3831] 3\n[3832] Is that really the case? Is it really like that? [3833] I tried to close my eyes and think. When Mr. Onizuka went downstairs, there were Higashizawa in the kitchen and Kikuko who returned to her room. There was also Akiyoshi, who was not in the kitchen and was not upstairs. Why was Higashizawa identified as the murderer? [3834] \"Why is it Higashizawa?\" I asked. [3835] \"Are you saying that Mrs. Mochizuki was also downstairs? If Mrs. Mochizuki was the murderer, what would have happened? She would have had to rush out of the bedroom without saying a word to her fianc\u00e9 and immediately spray perfume on the items. If Mrs. Mochizuki was the murderer, how could she do such a thing without disturbing Higashizawa in the kitchen?\" [3836]\"...\"\n[3837]\"Higuchi said, 'When I was washing dishes, Mr. Ono came downstairs humming a song and left immediately.' This is true. It would be too foolish to fabricate Mrs. Mochizuki rushing out from inside and doing such a thing; if his testimony mentioned 