ei answered immediately. \"Isn't the umbrella found at the crime scene also emitting a scent from the inside?\" [3850] \"Oh, I see\u2026\"\n[3851] \"The killer would carefully spray perfume on the object first... even if it's not enough to cover the body... The reason is here. To hide the unnaturalness of the umbrella emitting a scent even on the inside, they sprayed perfume from the whole umbrella, even the inside of the suitcase.\" [3852] That's why there wasn't enough perfume to cover the head! That's one of the pieces of the puzzle. [3853] However, there are still several pieces of the puzzle that don't fit. Why did the killer deliberately lift the body to the rock shelf? Why did he cut off the right ear? The answers to these questions are still unclear. [3854] Just as I was thinking this, the Jiang dean continued his explanation - although not the answers to the questions I had in mind. [3855] \"After killing Mr. Onizuka and returning to the mansion, Yaezawa probably discovered something when he entered the entrance hall. Or it was something he expected.\" [3856] \"What was it?\" [3857] \"The scent of the perfume left on the umbrella.\" [3858] I imagined eight-moku-zan sneaking back into the main house after committing the terrible crime. The entrance hall was filled with the smell of \"bou-sai,\" the same scent of perfume left at the crime scene. I suddenly felt the sweet smell of death on my nose. [3859] However, I had never smelled the scent of \"bou-sai\" drifting through the entrance hall. I smelled a different scent. [3860] \"So... the scent I smelled in the middle of the night, a mixture of 'enigme' and 'fauve', was... \"\n[3861] \"That was Hakamura sprinkling on to cover up the remaining scent of 'Bog Tree'. Your discovery in the entrance hall proves this. Sprinkling two perfumes would be a precautionary measure in case the 'Bog Tree' scent alone could be detected.\" [3862] \"But why would Hakamura want to hide the remaining 'Bog Tree' scent in the entr