d on the ground. My throat was as dry as the moon's surface, and I couldn't even swallow my saliva. [2730] \"Kakigawa, are you okay?\" Oyamada asked me. [2731] I replied, \"Yeah, I'm fine.\" - actually, I was not at all fine, but I could still stand. [2732] \"Call the police right away! Luckily, the phone was restored by evening.\" [2733] Yokozawa immediately said, \"And also ask Midori doctor to come. Even if it's confirmed that Suzu really died, it will take the forensic doctor several hours to get here\u2026\"\n[2734] Ochiai quickly made a decision, \"Let's do it! Let's borrow Midori doctor's phone to contact the police! It's faster this way.\" We ran out of the abandoned school. All the way, I wondered why the photographer was killed? Why kill an outsider? By thinking about something, I could temporarily forget the dead man's face. [2735] Fortunately, Mashiro was not here. I thanked this for the first time. [2736] The Uesugi house is still lit, but the clinic is still pitch black, just like before. Dr. Nakahara must have gone to sleep already. Despite feeling apologetic, I still pressed the doorbell. A few minutes later, just as I was about to press the button again, a figure appeared on the other side of the frosted glass. [2737] \"What's wrong? Is someone sick?\" asked the doctor, wearing a cotton coat over his pajamas with a sleepy voice. [2738] I met his gaze, \"Doctor, please come with us to the classroom of the elementary school! Mr. Nagaura has had an accident and is no longer moving!\" [2739] I must explain everything clearly! [2740] \"He's lying on the ground, completely still, and he's dead.\" [2741] Be more specific! [2742] \"It seems like he was murdered. He was strangled.\" [2743] Doctor Nakagawa looked at me curiously, \"That photographer was murdered? In the elementary school classroom? Are you joking with me?\" [2744] \"We wouldn't joke around at this late hour. Just come and see for yourself. By the way, Doctor, can I borrow your phone? I need to call the police.\" [2745] After seeing our unusual way of speaking and hearing the phrase \"call the police,\" Doctor Nakagawa finally believed us. [2746] \"The phone is here.\" [2747] He leads us to the examination room, looks up the phone book, and tells us the phone number for the Sagamori Police Station. [2748] This is the first time I have ever called the police in my life. I don't even have time to think about what to say first when I hear a rough male voice say, \"I'm the police.\" [2749] Oh! So that's how the police answer the phone! I marvel at this strange thing, but I can't say anything for a moment. [2750] \"Hello?\" [2751] \"Ah...um...I'm calling from Sumizu village. We found an unusual corpse that seems to be a murder case.\" [2752] \"Where are you calling from? May I know your full name, please?\" [2753] Ugh! Why are you so calm, police officer? Although, maybe there's nothing particularly bad about that...\n[2754] \"My name is Uzuki Uzuki. I'm using the phone at the Sumizu village clinic.\" [2755] \"Uzuki-san... How do you pronounce that?\" [2756] Oh no! I shouldn't have come to report an emergency with such an unusual name. [2757] \"Don't give your full name!\" Wakamatsu muttered next to me. [2758] I repeated myself: \"My surname is Yukiya.\" [2759] \"You said you found a corpse in Xiangsen Village, right? Where in the village?\" [2760] \"In the abandoned classroom of Xiangsen Village. Please come over immediately.\" [2761] \"Wait. What do you mean by 'strange' about the body?\" [2762] \"There are signs of strangulation. It was neither an accident nor suicide.\" [2763] \"Understood. Please wait a moment online.\" [2764] Why do I have to wait? It's strange. Everyone around me is surprised that I'm not talking. Just as I'm about to explain, the gruff voice speaks up again. [2765] \"I'm sorry to keep you waiting. Is Dr. Nakagawa at the clinic?\" [2766] \"Yes.\" [2767] \"Can you please give me the phone?\" [2768] \"Sure.\" I hand the receiver to Dr. N