e he used to teach, he can't just stay away. [2785] So, the five of us rush to the abandoned school. As we run, I inadvertently look up at the sky and see an anomaly. No, that's not right. I'm just a bit surprised. The moon is peeping out from behind the clouds, watching over us. [2786] 2\n[2787] \"The time of death is probably four to six hours ago!\" Nakauchi was still squatting next to the corpse. [2788] Mr. Higisawa and the three of us stood shoulder to shoulder in the corridor, looking out the window at Nakauchi's examination. What was going on? I never thought I'd be here, watching such a situation. [2789] \"It seems to have been strangled by a rope-like thing and suffocated to death. I don't know where the rope is, and finding it is the job of the police. For me, all I can confirm is that.\" Nakauchi stood up and stretched lazily. [2790] \"That's enough information,\" Mr. Higisawa said from the window. \"Four to six hours... so he was killed between 7 and 9 pm last night! If it had been investigated in the morning, the range of estimated time of death would have been much larger. The police are really clever to have commissioned a doctor to conduct an autopsy!\" [2791] \"No wonder they trust Dr. Nakahara.\" [2792] Dr. Nakahara shook his head, sighing as he walked down the corridor. He lit a cigarette and said, \"Let's go to the room.\" [2793] Following his suggestion, we went to the adjacent classroom and sat on the cold chairs. The chairs were designed for small children, leaving our butts hanging out and covered in dust. For some reason, Dr. Nakahara habitually pressed the light switch, even though he knew it wouldn't work. [2794] \"Dr. Nakahara, it won't turn on!\" Yoshima said, and the doctor smiled ruefully, sitting down on the nearest chair. [2795] \"Nevertheless, what is going on? How could a tragedy like this befall Yagihara? It doesn't seem like a robbery!\" Yoshima said. \"Exactly!\" Dr. Nakahara said, flicking ash from his cigarette, \"I can't imagine he was robbed, nor can I imagine who might have had a grudge against him. After all, there aren't many people in this village who even spoke to him!\" [2796] \"That's right! What's going on here?\" Yuki crossed his legs and pondered. [2797] I think there's no hatred in this village towards Sugata, let alone someone who hates him so much that they want to kill him. Sugata, who peeped into Komori Village, didn't do anything bad in this village, he was just a passerby. Besides us, there are only a few people who have had contact with him, including Mr. Nakagawa, Mei, the innkeeper, the owner of Fukuju, and Mr. Nishimura who came yesterday afternoon. Although Mr. Yuki and the post office employees, Roomi, should have met him... I can't think of anyone else, but are there really people among them who have been driven to kill him? [2798] Wait, there's someone who had contact with Sugata but wasn't very friendly - the villagers of Komori Village. I remember the one who grabbed his wrist and chased him out when Sugata illegally entered - Higashino. Hmm, besides Higashino, there should be other villagers who felt strongly angry about Sugata's actions, such as the poet Shoji Taj\u014dmaru... It's not Taj\u014dmaru, because he didn't seem angry when he mentioned Sugata. Maybe it's one of the other unknown people who fought with us in the rain... Oh! [2799] Could it be Chiaki Miyoshi? She not only left the entertainment industry but also escaped the world, living sadly in Komori Village. In her eyes, Sugata should be like this - a stubborn wolf that is obsessed with her. So, Sugata must have been hated. Will Chiaki get fixated and have the thought of killing him? Well, that's unknown...\n[2800] Wait, I just thought of something, so I couldn't help but put my hand on my forehead. Although there are people in Komori Village who dislike Sugata, the killer should not be among them. Because the bridge over the Tateno River was broken at around 11:30 am yesterday. After that, the