mes, Mei answered the phone. [4606] \"This is Miyuki.\" [4607] \"This is Yuki. Sorry for calling so late.\" [4608] \"Hmm.\" [4609] Her voice sounded weak. Is she still not feeling well, or has she already gone to bed? I'm worried. [4610] \"Can I talk to you?\" [4611] \"Yes.\" [4612] Another short answer. But since she said \"Yes,\" I'll go ahead and say it. [4613] \"The situation has taken a sudden turn, so I called you. I heard that Mr. Shibuki ran away!\" [4614] \"Ran away?\" [4615] Hearing this news suddenly, she probably didn't understand what was going on, so I'll briefly explain the situation again. Throughout this, she didn't interrupt with any questions, only softly responding with \"Hmm, hmm.\" [4616] \"So, it was Mr. Mukuro who was the culprit!\" [4617] The other end of the line fell silent. This was similar to our reaction just now. [4618] \"So that's how it is\u2026\"\n[4619] Her voice still sounded weak and powerless, causing me to worry, \"Are you still not feeling well?\" [4620] \"No, I'm fine.\" [4621] \"Really?\" [4622] Perhaps my whispering into the phone was too strange, as I heard Wakayama's voice behind me, \"That creep is at it again!\" [4623] \"Don't worry, it's okay.\" [4624] \"Really? Sorry, I was too nosy.\" [4625] \"No, you're so gentle, Higashikata-san.\" [4626] I could see a smile on her lips. [4627] \"No...it's nothing.\" [4628] \"I'm so jealous of Miyabi!\" [4629] I was at a loss for words. So far, there have been similar misunderstandings, and it seems that Miyabi is also mistaken. In fact, Miyabi and I are just friends with a boyfriend-girlfriend name, and the depth of our relationship is even less than a phone card. It's amazing that there are still many people who can't see this point. Miyabi has never seen me walking side by side with me, so this is probably just her innocent speculation. [4630] \"You seem to have misunderstood something.\" [4631] The response this time was: \"Oh, you're shy?\" [4632] This made my mood confused. I'm twenty years old, and I'm still so innocent? Thinking this, I couldn't help but laugh. [4633] \"Well... Shirogane-san is currently on the run. It seems that someone has gone to the mountains to catch him.\" [4634] \"It's really serious!\" [4635] Since her voice still lacked spirit, I judged that this phone call must still have disturbed her, so I decided to stop here. \"I'm sorry for disturbing you while you're resting...\"\n[4636] \"It's okay, don't say that. Thank you for letting me know. That's all for now.\" [4637] \"Goodnight.\" As I hung up the phone, I regretted making this call. It reminded me of Miyuki again. [4638] 2\n[4639] \"I should be leaving now. I've stayed for too long.\" Yoshino stood up with her handbag under her arm, but suddenly hesitated, \"I didn't realize there was school tomorrow. I drank too much...\"\n[4640] Yoshino was indeed drunk, and her walk was already slanted. [4641] Nishijima went back to his room. [4642] We helped Yuri-sensei down the stairs by putting our hands on his shoulders. [4643] \"That's far enough.\" As he spoke, Yuri stumbled, hitting his head on the entrance door. We couldn't just leave him, so we walked him outside together. [4644] \"Ah, this is the cool night air! It's so refreshing!\" Yuri spread his hands and took a deep breath. [4645] However, this was not a peaceful night. Several police cars with sirens blared over the mountain roads, heading towards us. More hunters had arrived. [4646] \"What a bother,\" said Feijiao, his eyes fixed on the direction of the sirens. His eyelids were half-opened, as if weighed down by a thousand pounds. [4647] We ignored Feijiao's refusal and insisted on taking him home. It was not out of kindness, but rather because we were concerned about what might happen in the village and wanted to take advantage of the opportunity to go outside. [4648] After saying goodnight to Feijiao at his house, we saw Nakatani Doctor peeking out of the clinic window. \"Wow, quite a commotion!\" [4649]